{"t": 1795503075.073477, "kind": "assistant", "text": "## Production decision: **NO-GO**\n\n- **Dev upgraded:** PHP 7.4.33 → **8.3.31**\n- **Snapshot created:** `dev/pre-php-8.3-security-upgrade-202.tgz`\n- **Home page:** still returns **500 (`php_fatal`)**\n- **Cause:** active plugin **`flexible-posts-widget` 3.4.1** calls the removed PHP function **`create_function()`**, making it incompatible with PHP 8.3.\n- **Production:** unchanged at PHP 7.4.33.\n\nI did **not** deactivate the plugin or edit any plugin files. An authorized maintainer must update or fix `flexible-posts-widget` for PHP 8.3, after which dev must be retested successfully before a production upgrade plan can be approved."}
